Cookie Policy
BokHus.com
Last updated: [insert date]
This Cookie Policy explains how BokHus.com uses cookies and similar technologies in accordance with the EU ePrivacy Directive and the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR).
By using BokHus.com, you consent to the use of cookies as described in this policy.

1. What Are Cookies
Cookies are small text files stored on your device when you visit a website.
They help websites:
remember user preferences
improve performance
analyze website traffic
enhance user experience
Cookies may be temporary (session cookies) or stored for longer periods (persistent cookies).

2. Types of Cookies We Use
Essential Cookies
These cookies are necessary for the website to function properly.
They may include:
security cookies
session management
login or form functionality
These cookies cannot be disabled because the website would not work properly without them.

Analytics Cookies
These cookies help us understand how visitors use the website.
They collect information such as:
pages visited
time spent on pages
navigation patterns
general geographic region
Examples may include:
Google Analytics
privacy-friendly analytics tools
The information collected is typically anonymized and used only for statistical purposes.

Functional Cookies
Functional cookies allow the website to remember user preferences, such as:
language settings
display preferences
saved options
These improve the user experience but are not strictly necessary.

Marketing Cookies (if applicable)
If BokHus.com uses marketing or social media integrations, cookies may be set by services such as:
Facebook
Instagram
advertising platforms
These cookies may track browsing behaviour to deliver relevant content or advertisements.
BokHus does not directly control these third-party cookies.

3. Third-Party Cookies
Some cookies may be set by third-party services integrated into the website, including:
analytics providers
embedded media
social media platforms
These providers may process data according to their own privacy policies.

4. Managing Cookies
You can manage or disable cookies through your browser settings.
Most browsers allow you to:
block cookies
delete stored cookies
receive warnings before cookies are stored
Instructions are usually available in your browser’s help section.
Please note that disabling cookies may affect the functionality of the website.

5. Cookie Consent
When you first visit BokHus.com, you may see a cookie consent banner that allows you to:
accept all cookies
reject non-essential cookies
customize cookie preferences
Your preferences can be changed at any time.

6. Data Protection
Cookies that process personal data are handled in accordance with our Privacy Policy and applicable data protection laws.

7. Updates to This Cookie Policy
We may update this Cookie Policy to reflect changes in legal requirements or website functionality.
Updated versions will be published on this page with a revised date.

